# The build context for this image is frontend/, so the repository root
# .dockerignore does not apply here.
node_modules
.next
out
.env*.local
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
Dockerfile

# Test files are deliberately NOT excluded. .dockerignore matches with Go's
# filepath.Match, so `*.test.tsx` matches only the context root and misses
# src/components/*.test.tsx — while `src/test/setup.ts`, which registers the
# jest-dom matchers, WAS excluded. `next build` then type-checked the tests
# without their matcher types and failed on ~30 TS2339 errors.
#
# Excluding them properly would mean `**/*.test.tsx` plus keeping that list in
# step with the vitest config forever, to save a few KB from a *build* stage.
# The runtime stage copies only .next/standalone, .next/static and public, so
# nothing here reaches the shipped image regardless. Letting the image build
# type-check exactly what CI type-checks is worth more than the KB.
